notations","l":"full","t":"Annotations","x":[]},{"a":["secrets.create (replication)","secrets.get"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.replication","l":"limited","t":"Replication policy (locations) and encryption (CMEK)","x":["The replication policy is validated the way the real API validates it (exactly one of automatic/userManaged, non-empty/unique userManaged locations, a well-formed CMEK key name whose location matches its replica) and is immutable after creation, but Vyomi keeps one copy of the payload — it does not physically replicate it across locations or encrypt it with the named Cloud KMS key."]},{"a":["secrets.create (rotation)","secrets.patch (rotation)"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.rotation","l":"limited","t":"Rotation","x":["Rotation is validated the way the real API validates it (a rotation period/nextRotationTime requires at least one configured Pub/Sub topic, a minimum 1-hour period, a future nextRotationTime), and removing the last topic while a rotation policy is active is rejected. Vyomi still does not run a rotation schedule or add versions automatically."]},{"a":["secrets.create (expireTime, ttl)","secrets.patch (expireTime, ttl)"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.expiration","l":"full","t":"Expiration","x":[]},{"a":["secrets.create (topics)","secrets.patch (topics)"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.notifications","l":"limited","t":"Notifications (Pub/Sub topics)","x":["Vyomi publishes a real Pub/Sub message to every configured topic on SECRET_VERSION_ADD/ENABLE/DISABLE/DESTROY (and on auto-expiry); it does not publish SECRET_ROTATE, since rotation itself isn't run on a schedule."]},{"a":["secrets.create (versionAliases)","secrets.patch (versionAliases)"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.version-aliases","l":"full","t":"Version aliases","x":[]},{"a":["secrets.getIamPolicy","secrets.setIamPolicy","secrets.testIamPermissions"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.permissions","l":"limited","t":"Permissions (IAM policy)","x":["getIamPolicy/setIamPolicy/testIamPermissions store a real per-secret policy that IS enforced (versions.access/add/enable/disable/destroy and secrets.update/delete/setIamPolicy are denied for a principal the policy doesn't grant); it covers a curated set of predefined roles and a single X-Cloudlearn-Principal header rather than Google's full role catalog and credential model."]},{"a":["logging.entries.list"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.logs","l":"limited","t":"Logs","x":["Secret create/version-add/enable/disable/destroy/delete/setIamPolicy/auto-expire events write a real Cloud Logging entry the Logs tab reads back (entries:list); read/access calls and the full Cloud Audit Log protoPayload shape aren't recorded."]},{"a":["secrets.create (locations)","secrets.get","secrets.list","secrets.delete","secrets.addVersion","versions.access","versions.enable","versions.disable","versions.destroy","secrets.getIamPolicy","secrets.setIamPolicy"],"id":"gcp.secret-manager.regional-secrets","l":"limited","t":"Regional secrets","x":["Regional secrets (projects/{p}/locations/{location}/secrets/...) are a distinct resource namespace from global secrets, with their own create/get/list/delete, version lifecycle (addVersion/access/enable/disable/destroy), labels/annotations/rotation/expiration/notifications/versionAliases and an enforced per-secret IAM policy — but Vyomi keeps one copy of the payload in the named location rather than running Google's dedicated regional infrastructure, and a customerManagedEncryption key is validated (shape + location match, immutable after creation) without being used to actually encrypt anything."]}],"id":"security/secret-manager","ops":32,"registry_unreachable":[],"title":"Secret Manager","total":36}
